{"timestamp": 1779388232.5547671, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I reported Alice in storage. My route was security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage. I saw Diana in navigation around ticks 7-9; she came in from security and was still there while I was around nav. I didn\u2019t see Alice alive this round, and I didn\u2019t see Charlie\u2019s body \u2014 apparently Charlie was in lower engine. I don\u2019t have an accusation yet, just that Alice was dead in storage when I arrived."}}
{"timestamp": 1779388241.876284, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I'll lay out my route: storage \u2192 medbay \u2192 storage \u2192 lower engine. In medbay early (ticks 3-4) I was with Alice and Frank. Frank left to electrical around tick 4, Alice left to storage at tick 5. I went back to storage and saw Alice there at tick 7 \u2014 she was alive then. After that I headed to lower engine where I found Charlie at tick 10 coming in from upper engine. He was alive when I left... well, we ended up in the same room and now he's dead, which looks bad for me, I won't lie. But think about it \u2014 if I killed Charlie, why would I sit there until the meeting? I didn't report because I was hoping to clear lower engine first.\n\nEve, you said Diana was in nav with you ticks 7-9. So Diana's somewhat covered for Alice's death if Alice was killed after tick 7 in storage. But what about Frank? He went to electrical at tick 4 and I have no idea where he went after. Frank, where were you between ticks 5 and 12?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779388272.4928691, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I was with Alice and Bob in medbay early. My route was medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 back through medbay \u2192 upper engine. Alice came into medbay from electrical at tick 1, Bob came in from storage at tick 3, and all three of us were in medbay around ticks 3-4. I left toward electrical around tick 4 like Bob said. After that I didn\u2019t see Alice, Bob, Charlie, Eve, or Diana again before the report.\n\nI never saw Charlie in upper engine, and there was no body there when I was there. So if Charlie came from upper engine into lower engine at tick 10 like Bob says, that was after my path or outside my vision.\n\nHonestly, Bob\u2019s story worries me the most right now: he says he saw Alice alive in storage at tick 7, then later was with Charlie in lower engine, and now both Alice and Charlie are dead. That puts Bob near both victims at the relevant times. I\u2019m not saying it\u2019s 100%, but that\u2019s the strongest connection so far. Diana being in nav with Eve around 7-9 makes her less likely for Alice unless timing is weird."}}
{"timestamp": 1779388302.700886, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I can confirm Eve\u2019s part about me: my route was weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 back to security. I saw Eve in security around tick 3, she left security to navigation at tick 4, then I saw her in navigation ticks 7 and 8. At tick 9 she left navigation toward storage, and I went back toward security. I didn\u2019t see Alice, Charlie, Bob, or Frank at all this round.\n\nSo for Alice: if Bob is telling the truth that Alice was alive in storage at tick 7, then Eve reached storage after leaving nav at tick 9 and found/reporting her there. That\u2019s possible, but Eve was with/near me right before that, so timing is tight unless it\u2019s a self-report. For Charlie: Bob is the only one placing himself with Charlie in lower engine, and Charlie is dead now. Also Bob saying he didn\u2019t report because he wanted to \u201cclear lower engine first\u201d feels really weird \u2014 if you see a body, you report.\n\nFrank is unaccounted for after electrical, but Bob has direct links to both dead players: saw Alice alive in storage, then was with Charlie in lower engine. I think Bob is the strongest vote here."}}
{"timestamp": 1779388324.9213388, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I\u2019m still on Bob as the strongest suspect.\n\nTo restate my route: security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage. Diana and I saw each other in/around navigation ticks 7-9, and she confirms I left nav toward storage at tick 9. I found Alice dead in storage when I arrived and reported immediately.\n\nThe big issue is Bob\u2019s story. He says he saw Alice alive in storage at tick 7, then later was with Charlie in lower engine, and now both Alice and Charlie are dead. Also, the \u201cI didn\u2019t report because I wanted to clear lower engine first\u201d line is really bad \u2014 if you see a body, you report it. That sounds like he was near Charlie\u2019s body and chose not to report.\n\nFrank is less cleared than Diana, but Bob has direct proximity to both deaths and his explanation has holes. I think Bob is the vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1779388336.802235, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Okay, I hear you all, and I get why I look bad on paper. Let me push back hard though, because the logic isn't as clean as Diana and Eve are making it sound.\n\nOn Alice: I said I saw her ALIVE in storage at tick 7. That's information I volunteered \u2014 if I killed her, why would I place myself in storage with her at all? I could have just said \"I went medbay then lower engine\" and you'd have nothing on me. I told you the truth because it's the truth.\n\nOn Charlie: Charlie walked into lower engine at tick 10 from upper engine. Frank just told you his route ended at upper engine. Frank, when exactly did you leave upper engine? Because if Charlie came from upper engine at tick 10, either Charlie was in upper engine with you, or he passed through right after you left. Either way, you're the last person connected to Charlie before me. You're saying you never saw him in upper engine \u2014 convenient, because it means you can't be tied to him. But the geography says otherwise.\n\nAnd yes, I admit \"wanting to clear lower engine first\" was a dumb instinct \u2014 I should have reported. But a Duck who just killed wouldn't sit on the body for two ticks waiting to get caught. I sat there because I was confused, not because I'm the killer.\n\nDiana and Eve alibi each other in nav/security. Frank has NO ONE confirming him after tick 4. He's the floater here. I think the real question is Frank, not me."}}
{"timestamp": 1779388389.432151, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Bob, I get why you\u2019re pushing back, but your defense doesn\u2019t really clear you.\n\nFirst: I did **not** leave upper engine \u2014 I was in upper engine when the meeting got called. My route was medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 back through medbay \u2192 upper engine. I never saw Charlie in upper engine, never saw him pass through, and there was no body there. So your claim that Charlie came from upper engine into lower engine is only coming from you.\n\nSecond: saying \u201cwhy would I admit I saw Alice alive in storage\u201d doesn\u2019t clear you. Ducks can give true info to control the timeline. The fact is: you were with Alice in medbay, then you say you saw her alive in storage at tick 7, and Eve finds Alice dead in storage shortly after. Then you\u2019re also the only person placing yourself with Charlie in lower engine before he dies.\n\nDiana and Eve have a mutual timeline around security/navigation. I\u2019m unconfirmed after tick 4, yes, but I have no direct link to Alice\u2019s body location and I never saw Charlie. You have direct proximity to both dead players, and the Charlie story depends entirely on us trusting you.\n\nI still think Bob is the strongest vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1779388407.3526669, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I\u2019m sticking with Bob here.\n\nMy info hasn\u2019t changed: I was weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 security. I saw Eve in security at tick 3, then she left toward nav at tick 4. I saw her again in navigation ticks 7-8, and at tick 9 she left toward storage. So Eve\u2019s report timing on Alice makes sense, and I don\u2019t think she had much time to kill Alice unless it\u2019s a very tight self-report.\n\nThe two biggest problems are still Bob\u2019s:\n\n1. He\u2019s the last person claiming to see Alice alive in storage, and Alice is then found dead in storage.\n2. He\u2019s also the only person claiming to be with Charlie in lower engine, and Charlie is dead too.\n3. The \u201cI didn\u2019t report because I wanted to clear lower engine first\u201d explanation is really bad. If you see a body, you report immediately.\n\nFrank is unconfirmed, but Bob is directly connected to both kills. I think voting Bob is the best call."}}
